# A CHAIN WITH ONE ASSERTED LEG AND ONE EXISTENTIAL LEG (SPEC 5.3 L4, L6).
# r ∘ s ⊑ t; r(a,b) is asserted; (∃s.E)(b) gives b an s-successor in E. So a has
# a t-successor in E, and ∃t.E ⊑ F makes a an F; G(a), F disjoint from G.
# Expect: INCONSISTENT (exit 1).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:E a owl:Class . :F a owl:Class . :G a owl:Class . :F owl:disjointWith :G .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty . :t a owl:ObjectProperty .
:t owl:propertyChainAxiom ( :r :s ) .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :t ; owl:someValuesFrom :E ] rdfs:subClassOf :F .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :G .
:b a owl:NamedIndividual , [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:someValuesFrom :E ] .
:a :r :b .
